# loop-read-streak-milestones: read-streak guard RED→GREEN reproduction fixture (task loop-read-streak-guard).
#
# Scenario: a worker burns consecutive native-READ tool calls (read/grep/find/ls only) past
# milestones k=1..3. Milestone k fires only when BOTH readCallCount >= 6k AND
# accumulatedActiveMs >= 5·60_000·k (env PI_SWARM_READ_STREAK_MS overrides the segment floor;
# the override lives in the LANE COMMAND, never in this fixture).
#
# Expected GREEN (detector landed): mid-run self-nudge after the 6th READ (milestone k=1),
# 12th (k=2), and 18th (k=3) — each nudge text (READ-STREAK marker family, milestone number,
# call count, active time) lands in the NEXT model request via turn_end custom_message +
# continue:true. Exactly 3 mid-run continuations; final turn stop.
# Expected RED (pre-code reproduction): transcript shows NO nudge text anywhere, zero extra
# requests — the run burns all 18 READs silently.
#
# Shape (20 turns; pacing keeps the active segment open — toolUse stops keep the run looping
# tool->tool without settling mid-block, so segment time accrues from scripted delayMs):
#   t1..t6:   6 READ calls (text + read toolcall, stopReason toolUse) -> milestone k=1 boundary
#   t7..t12:  6 more READs -> k=2 boundary
#   t13..t18: 6 more READs -> k=3 boundary
#   t19:      text, toolUse (loop still running — the guard must NOT re-fire for k=1..3)
#   t20:      text, stopReason stop -> terminal settle
# Every delayMs is 15–25ms; all tool names are lowercase pi-builtin (read).
